Package: mvbcfMT
Type: Package
Title: Multi-Treatment Multivariate Bayesian Causal Forests
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Danilo A.", "Sarti", email = "danilo.stats@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = c("Alternative e-mail: danilosarti@rcsi.ie"))
Description: Estimates the joint causal effect of two or more crossed binary
    treatments on several correlated continuous outcomes at once, extending the
    single-treatment multivariate Bayesian causal forest to the full factorial of
    the crossed treatments. The factorial response surface is decomposed over the
    treatment lattice into
    a prognostic sum-of-trees forest and one forest per main or interaction
    effect, sharing an inverse-Wishart residual covariance across outcomes. A
    single unified 'Rcpp' engine samples every component; the two-treatment model
    is the order-two, two-treatment special case, and a general order-r truncation
    handles more treatments. The package provides per-treatment propensity
    adjustment, per-component effect and interaction estimands with credible
    intervals, a cross-fitted debiased (one-step) average-effect estimator with
    efficient standard errors, positivity and unmeasured-confounding diagnostics,
    and value-suppressing uncertainty visualisations of the interaction surface.
